# WordPress PHP (theme `functions.php` or preferably `mu-plugins/`)

This repo is the Next.js client. PHP below is the contract WordPress must implement.
Canonical copies live in `docs/wordpress/`:

- `crilio-cart-handoff.php` — §5 cart handoff
- `crilio-headless-bridge.php` — §6 routing, §6a CORS, Crilio checkout/account skin

**Do not install:** Headless Mode plugin, WPGraphQL CORS plugin.

Set storefront URL in `wp-config.php` for production:

```php
define( 'CRILIO_STOREFRONT_URL', 'https://yourperfume.com' );
```

## §5 Cart handoff (`wp_loaded`)

Listen for `$_GET['add-to-cart-custom']` (`parent_id:variation_id:quantity` comma-separated).

1. `WC()->cart->empty_cart()`
2. Parse items; for each call `WC()->cart->add_to_cart( $product_id, $quantity, $variation_id )`
3. `wp_safe_redirect( wc_get_checkout_url() ); exit;`

Next.js builds this URL via `buildCheckoutHandoffUrl` — keep the query shape identical. No multi-cart plugins.

## §6 Headless traffic routing (`template_redirect`)

Allow native load (no redirect) when any of:

- `is_admin()`
- `is_cart()`
- `is_checkout()`
- `is_account_page()`
- `wp_doing_ajax()`
- GraphQL API endpoint request

All other frontend requests: `wp_redirect( 'https://<vercel-storefront-domain>', 301 ); exit;`

## §6a GraphQL CORS (no plugin)

Whitelist only:

- Production Vercel origin (e.g. `https://yourperfume.com`)
- `http://localhost:3000`

Prefer `graphql_response_headers_to_send`. Handle OPTIONS preflight. Never use `*`. Server-side Next.js `fetch` does not need CORS; this is for browser-origin GraphQL.
